\boxed{5}

Reasoning: Since \( Q \) is on the line segment \( CD \) and minimizing the distance to \( A(1, 1) \), the ideal position would be \( Q \) coinciding with \( C \) (as \( Q \) cannot directly coincide with \( D \) and be closer to \( A \)). However, since \( Q \) should lie within \( CD \), making the correct \( x \)-coordinate \( 5 \) (identical to \( C \)) is the \emph{closed optimal} solution.

